self_cause	one
prior_self	one
infinite	one
first	two	first	P6 C	a cause standing before the intermediate causes in a given series, which each intermediate needs	an uncaused cause that begins the whole series, with nothing before it
intermediate	one
ultimate	one
# first: P4, P5 and C2 are true only if "first" means a preceding cause of the intermediate. An infinite series has such a cause for every member, so it does not lack a first in this sense.
# P6 is true only if "first" means absolutely uncaused, and C asserts a first cause in that sense.
